{"step_index":4279,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T23:39:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-23T02:39:35+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-23T02:39:35+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/src/fast_match/coordinator.py`\nTotal Lines: 363\nTotal Bytes: 19928\nShowing lines 1 to 55\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import json\n2: import time\n3: import re\n4: import concurrent.futures\n5: import requests as http_requests\n6: \n7: from ..config import Config\n8: from .search import FastCandidateFinder, extract_form_group, extract_brand_tokens\n9: from ..match.text_match import normalize_text\n10: from rapidfuzz import fuzz\n11: \n12: \n13: SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are an expert clinical and Egyptian pharmaceutical matching assistant.\n14: You match requested drug names from pharmacy shortages with candidate items available in wholesale drug warehouses.\n15: \n16: CRITICAL PHARMACEUTICAL RULES:\n17: 1. STRICT BRAND IDENTITY (NO GENERICS / NO ALTERNATIVES):\n18:    - You MUST match the EXACT SAME commercial trade brand name.\n19:    - NEVER suggest or accept alternative brand names, different trade names, or generics (e.g. Panadol is NOT Cetal, Brufen is NOT Cataflam, Augmentin is NOT Curam).\n20:    - If the trade brand name is different, unrelated, or an alternative product, YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\" (or omit it). NEVER mark different brands as \"match\" or \"review\"!\n21:    - Distinct commercial prefixes (like \"نيو\" / \"New\") or distinct trade endings (like \"-يتش\" vs \"-ين\") signify different trade brands (e.g. New Carbon is NOT Eucarbon, Protoloc is NOT Controloc, Skinoren is NOT Skinorich, Grantril is NOT Grantil). Return \"no_match\".\n22:    - Allow ONLY minor spelling variants, phonetic transliterations, or common OCR scanning typos of the SAME exact brand (e.g. dropped initial letters like 'ا', dropped middle single letters or missing dots like 'ن' or 'ب' e.g. 'فتال' for 'فنتال', visually confused OCR letters like 'ف' vs 'د' e.g. 'سيفيتيل' vs 'سيديتيل', or slight vowel variations).\n23: \n24: 2. DOSAGE FORM & FORMULATION (ZERO TOLERANCE FOR CONFLICTS):\n25:    - Dosage forms MUST be strictly compatible:\n26:      - Tablets/Capsules (اقراص, كبسول, حبوب, فيلم, شريط) ONLY match Tablets/Capsules.\n27:      - Syrups/Suspensions (شراب, شرب, معلق) ONLY match Syrups. NEVER match tablets with syrup.\n28:      - Creams (كريم) ONLY match Creams. NEVER match cream with ointment or suppository.\n29:      - Ointments (مرهم, دهان) ONLY match Ointments.\n30:      - Injections/Ampoules (امبول, حقن, فيال) ONLY match Injections.\n31:      - Suppositories (لبوس) ONLY match Suppositories.\n32:      - Drops (نقط, قطرة) ONLY match Drops.\n33:      - Sprays (بخاخ, سبراي) ONLY match Sprays.\n34:    - COMBINATION PRODUCTS (Zero Tolerance): Commercial suffixes like \"كو\" (Co), \"كومب\" (Comp), \"بلس\" (Plus) denote a multi-ingredient combination product (e.g. adding a diuretic or vitamin). A combination product (e.g. 'سينوبريل كو') MUST NEVER match a single-ingredient plain product ('سينوبريل'). Return \"no_match\".\n35:    - If dosage forms or combination types conflict, YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n36: \n37: 3. STRENGTH / CONCENTRATION (ZERO TOLERANCE FOR MISMATCH):\n38:    - If the requested drug specifies a strength (e.g. 457mg, 600mg, 500mg, 1000mg/1gm, 20mg, 40mg) and the candidate has a DIFFERENT numeric strength:\n39:      YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n40:    - Note vernacular and fractional equivalencies:\n41:      - 1000mg = 1gm (1000مجم = 1جم).\n42:      - 500mg = 0.5gm = نص (نصف).\n43:      - 0.25mg = 250mcg = 25. مجم = ربع (e.g. 'بالموكورت 25. مجم' is identical to 'بالميكورت ربع').\n44: \n45: 4. PACKAGING, PACK SIZE & WHOLESALE UNITS (MATCH vs REVIEW):\n46:    - \"match\": Same brand, same form, same strength.\n47:      - STANDARD PACKS: If requested shortage specifies standard packaging count (e.g. 20 tablets, 5 ampoules, 3 strips) and warehouse candidate has the same drug, form, and strength but does not explicitly state the pack size (e.g. standard listing without count):\n48:        THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")! NEVER mark this as review!\n49:      - STRIP-TO-TABLET EQUIVALENCE: When a shortage requests standard blisters/strips (e.g. 3 شريط) and the warehouse lists the standard full pack tablet count for that drug (e.g. 12 tablets where each strip has 4 tablets, like فايركتا), this is a 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\n50:      - Manufacturer suffixes (/فاركو, /جلاكسو), commercial indicators (\"س ج\", \"سعر جديد\", \"سعر قديم\") do not change the product.\n51:    - \"review\": For the SAME EXACT medicine brand when there is an EXPLICIT, CONFLICTING pack count on BOTH sides (e.g. requested 30 tablets vs candidate explicitly writes 20 tablets of the same medicine).\n52:      - Wholesale packaging: If requested specifies retail strips/units (e.g. 2 شريط, 20 قرص) and warehouse specifies wholesale bundles/cartons (باكت / كرتونة / 32ب), mark as \"review\" with the reason explaining the wholesale packaging difference.\n53:      - CRITICAL SAFETY: When the trade brand name, form, and strength are identical, NEVER discard as \"no_match\" just because tablet/pack counts differ! It MUST be marked as \"review\" with the reason explaining the packaging difference.\n54:      - Wholesale bundles like \"باكت 120\" (meaning a shipping carton of 120 boxes) or \"باكت 50\" are wholesale lot sizes, NOT the blister/tablet count inside a single box! Do not confuse wholesale carton count with tablet count.\n55: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view