dosage forms or combination types conflict, YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n\n 3. STRENGTH / CONCENTRATION (ZERO TOLERANCE FOR MISMATCH):\n    - If the requested drug specifies a strength (e.g. 457mg, 600mg, 500mg, 1000mg/1gm, 20mg, 40mg) and the candidate has a DIFFERENT numeric strength:\n      YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n    - Note vernacular and fractional equivalencies:\n      - 1000mg = 1gm (1000مجم = 1جم).\n      - 500mg = 0.5gm = نص (نصف).\n      - 0.25mg = 250mcg = 25. مجم = ربع (e.g. \"ربع\" equals 0.25mg / 250mcg).\n\n 4. PACKAGING, PACK SIZE & WHOLESALE UNITS (MATCH vs REVIEW):\n    - \"match\": Same brand, same form, same strength.\n      - STANDARD PACKS: If requested shortage specifies standard packaging count (e.g. 20 tablets, 5 ampoules, 3 strips) and warehouse candidate has the same drug, form, and strength but does not explicitly state the pack size (e.g. standard listing without count):\n        THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")! NEVER mark this as review!\n      - STRIP-TO-TABLET EQUIVALENCE: When a shortage requests standard blisters/strips (e.g. 3 شريط) and the warehouse lists the standard full pack tablet count for that drug (e.g. 12 tablets where each strip contains 4 tablets), this is a 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\n      - Manufacturer suffixes (/فاركو, /جلاكسو), commercial indicators (\"س ج\", \"سعر جديد\", \"سعر قديم\") do not change the product.","StartLine":21,"TargetContent":"    - Distinct commercial prefixes (like \"نيو\" / \"New\") or distinct trade endings (like \"-يتش\" vs \"-ين\") signify different trade brands (e.g. New Carbon is NOT Eucarbon, Protoloc is NOT Controloc, Skinoren is NOT Skinorich, Grantril is NOT Grantil). Return \"no_match\".\n    - Allow ONLY minor spelling variants, phonetic transliterations, or common OCR scanning typos of the SAME exact brand (e.g. dropped initial letters like 'ا', dropped middle single letters or missing dots like 'ن' or 'ب' e.g. 'فتال' for 'فنتا